---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SpecTable from '../components/SpecTable.astro';
import CartridgeCard from '../components/CartridgeCard.astro';
import FaqSchema from '../components/FaqSchema.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Illinois Deer Season Dates 2026-27"
  description="Illinois's 2026-27 deer season dates, permit costs, and rifle rules — archery, firearm, muzzleloader, and youth season, all in one place, updated yearly."
>
  <section class="pillar">
    <div class="wrap pillar__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Season Dates — Illinois</p>
      <h1>Illinois Deer Season Dates: 2026-27</h1>
      <p class="pillar__intro">
        Illinois' 2026-27 deer firearm seasons are Nov. 20–22 and Dec. 3–6, 2026. Archery runs Oct. 1, 2026–Jan. 17, 2027 and muzzleloader is Dec. 11–13. Illinois caps hunters at two antlered bucks per year. This isn't a dated field note; we refresh it in
        place each year when the DNR publishes new dates.
      </p>
      <p class="pillar__updated">Last updated: October 1, 2026</p>

      <h2>2026-27 Illinois Deer Season Dates at a Glance</h2>

      <SpecTable
        caption="Illinois Deer Season Dates — 2026-27"
        compareColumns={["2026-27"]}
        metricRows={[
          { label: "Archery", values: ["Oct. 1, 2026 – Jan. 17, 2027"] },
          { label: "Youth Season", values: ["Oct. 10–12, 2026"] },
          { label: "Firearm Segment 1", values: ["Nov. 20–22, 2026"] },
          { label: "Firearm Segment 2", values: ["Dec. 3–6, 2026"] },
          { label: "Muzzleloader", values: ["Dec. 11–13, 2026"] },
          { label: "Bag Limit", values: ["No numeric total — 2 antlered bucks/yr cap"] },
        ]}
        note="Source: Illinois DNR's deer hunting, archery, and firearm/muzzleloader pages. Archery is closed in firearm counties during their local firearm segments."
      />

      <h2>Illinois' Two-Buck Cap and Lottery Permits</h2>
      <p>
        Illinois runs deer permits through a multi-round lottery for both residents and
        nonresidents rather than an open license — three lottery windows ran in 2026, the last
        from July 13 through August 21, with remaining county-specific permits going over the
        counter starting October 20 once quotas are filled.
      </p>
      <p>
        The bag limit works differently than most of its neighbors: there's <strong>no statewide
        numeric limit on total deer</strong>, but hunters are capped at <strong>two antlered
        bucks per year across all seasons combined</strong> (a Special CWD season in select
        counties is the one exception that allows additional antlered deer). See our <a href="/blog/chronic-wasting-disease-explained/">CWD explainer</a> if
        you're hunting inside one of those zones.
      </p>

      <h2>Can You Hunt With a Straight-Wall Cartridge in Illinois?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes — it's one of two qualifying case shapes, not the only one. Since a 2023 law change,
        Illinois allows single-shot centerfire rifles statewide in any county with a firearm
        deer season, straight-wall or bottleneck, as long as they clear the caliber and energy
        minimums.
      </p>
      <CartridgeCard
        name="Illinois"
        url="https://dnr.illinois.gov/hunting/deer/legal-cartridges.html"
        linkRel="noopener"
        description="Single-shot centerfire rifles only (2023 law) — but not straight-wall-only: .30 caliber+ straight-wall or .30 caliber+ bottleneck (case ≤1.4in) both qualify, at 500+ ft-lbs muzzle energy. Legal statewide in any county with a firearm season — not limited to a special list of counties. Changes again Jan. 1, 2027, when the single-shot limit lifts to a 3-round magazine/chamber combined."
        stats={[
          { label: "Case Shape", value: "Not required (bottleneck OK)" },
          { label: "Platform", value: "Single-shot through 2026" },
        ]}
      />
      <p>
        Want to see how your cartridge actually flies? Try our <a href="/ballistics-comparison/">ballistics comparison tool</a> or read <a href="/blog/straight-wall-vs-shouldered-ballistics-comparison/">Straight-Wall vs Shouldered Ballistics</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Weighing a straight-wall rifle against a modern muzzleloader instead? Illinois'
        FireStick-style muzzleloader status is still unconfirmed as of our last check — see our <a href="/blog/firestick-nitrofire-muzzleloader-legality-2026/">FireStick &amp; NitroFire legality guide</a> for
        the latest, and our <a href="/blog/straight-wall-cartridge-state-regulations/">straight-wall cartridge regulations guide</a> for
        how Illinois compares to the other six states in this region.
      </p>

      <h2>Illinois Deer Permit Costs, 2026-27</h2>
      <p>
        Illinois is the hardest state in this group to give a single price, since almost
        everything runs through a lottery. A resident hunting license is $12.50, and archery
        either-sex permits have run in the $17–$25.50 range depending on the lottery round and
        county.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nonresidents pay $57.75 for the license, with firearm either-sex permits landing around
        $300 after a successful draw (archery landowner permits run closer to $210). Hunter
        education is required for anyone born on or after Jan. 1, 1980.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the full seven-state cost and lottery breakdown — including how Illinois stacks up
        against Ohio, Michigan, Indiana, Iowa, Minnesota, and Wisconsin — see our <a href="/blog/deer-hunting-license-guide-seven-state/">Deer Hunting License Guide: 7-State Corn Belt Edition</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Plan Your Whole Illinois Season</h2>
      <p>
        A few more things worth lining up against the dates above before opening day:
      </p>
      <ul class="pillar__crosslinks">
        <li><a href="/blog/firestick-nitrofire-muzzleloader-legality-2026/">FireStick &amp; NitroFire Muzzleloaders: Legal States 2026-27</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/food-plot-or-mineral-site-leased-ground/">Food Plot vs. Mineral Site: Deer Hunting Laws by State</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/2026-deer-season-regulations-seven-state-roundup/">2026 Deer Season Regulations: 7-State Bag Limits Guide</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>More Corn Belt Season-Date Guides</h2>
      <ul class="pillar__crosslinks pillar__hub">
        <li><a href="/ohio-deer-season-dates/">Ohio Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/michigan-deer-season-dates/">Michigan Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/indiana-deer-season-dates/">Indiana Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/iowa-deer-season-dates/">Iowa Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/minnesota-deer-season-dates/">Minnesota Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/wisconsin-deer-season-dates/">Wisconsin Deer Season Dates</a></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="pillar__cta">
        <picture class="pillar__cta-cover">
          <source srcset="/images/perfect-window-cover.webp" type="image/webp" />
          <img src="/images/perfect-window-cover.jpg" alt="The Perfect Window book cover" width="500" height="647" loading="lazy" />
        </picture>
        <div class="pillar__cta-body">
          <p class="pillar__cta-title">Want every state's dates in one place?</p>
          <p class="pillar__cta-desc">
            <em>The Perfect Window</em> lays out harvest timing, rut windows, and legal season
            dates across all 12 Corn Belt states on one visual overlap chart — handy if you hunt
            more than just Illinois.
          </p>
          <a class="pillar__cta-link" href="https://link.amazon/B03KhoZDf" rel="sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Get it on Amazon &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>FAQ</h2>

      <p><strong>Is Illinois a straight-wall cartridge state?</strong><br />
      Yes, but it's not the only legal option. A .30-caliber-or-larger straight-wall or bottleneck
      single-shot rifle (case ≤1.4" for bottleneck), at 500+ ft-lbs of muzzle energy, is legal
      statewide in any county with a firearm season.</p>

      <p><strong>When does Illinois's 2026-27 deer archery season start?</strong><br />
      Thursday, Oct. 1, 2026, running through Sunday, Jan. 17, 2027 (closed in firearm counties
      during their local firearm segments).</p>

      <p><strong>What's Illinois's deer bag limit?</strong><br />
      No statewide numeric total, but hunters are capped at two antlered bucks per year across
      all seasons combined.</p>

      <p><strong>How much does an Illinois deer permit cost?</strong><br />
      A resident hunting license is $12.50, with archery permits running $17–$25.50 depending on
      the lottery round. Nonresidents pay $57.75 for the license, with firearm permits landing
      around $300 after a successful draw.</p>

      <FaqSchema items={[
        { question: "Is Illinois a straight-wall cartridge state?", answer: "Yes, but it's not the only legal option. A .30-caliber-or-larger straight-wall or bottleneck single-shot rifle (case 1.4in or less for bottleneck), at 500+ ft-lbs of muzzle energy, is legal statewide in any county with a firearm season." },
        { question: "When does Illinois's 2026-27 deer archery season start?", answer: "Thursday, Oct. 1, 2026, running through Sunday, Jan. 17, 2027 (closed in firearm counties during their local firearm segments)." },
        { question: "What's Illinois's deer bag limit?", answer: "No statewide numeric total, but hunters are capped at two antlered bucks per year across all seasons combined." },
        { question: "How much does an Illinois deer permit cost?", answer: "A resident hunting license is $12.50, with archery permits running $17-$25.50 depending on the lottery round. Nonresidents pay $57.75 for the license, with firearm permits landing around $300 after a successful draw." }
      ]} />
      <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "WebPage",
        name: "Illinois Deer Season Dates 2026-27",
        url: "https://cornfedbucks.com/illinois-deer-season-dates/",
        dateModified: "2026-10-01",
        inLanguage: "en-US",
        isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", name: "CornfedBucks", url: "https://cornfedbucks.com/" },
        author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Nick" }
      })} />

      <p class="pillar__disclaimer">
        Season dates and cartridge rules sourced from Illinois DNR's deer hunting, archery, and
        legal-cartridges pages. County- or zone-level exceptions can override anything listed
        here — always confirm current rules at <a href="https://dnr.illinois.gov/hunting/deerhunting.html" rel="noopener" target="_blank">dnr.illinois.gov</a> before
        you apply for a permit or head afield.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .pillar { padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .pillar__inner { max-width: 720px; }
  .pillar h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .pillar__intro {
    color: var(--ink);
    opacity: 0.85;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
  }
  .pillar .pillar__updated {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--stalk);
    margin: -1.1rem 0 1.75rem;
  }
  .pillar h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.6rem);
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .pillar p {
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .pillar__crosslinks {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .pillar__cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--husk);
    border: 1px solid var(--stalk);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 2.25rem;
  }
  .pillar__cta-cover { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 84px; }
  .pillar__cta-cover img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 3px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(34, 27, 20, 0.25);
  }
  .pillar__cta-body { min-width: 0; }
  .pillar__cta-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }
  .pillar__cta-desc { font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .pillar__cta-link {
    font-family: var(--font-tag);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--blaze);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .pillar__cta-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .pillar__cta { flex-direction: column; }
    .pillar__cta-cover { width: 100px; }
  }

  .pillar__disclaimer {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--stalk);
    line-height: 1.6;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--husk);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
